 available but disabled. "available" = currently loadable on this site (regardless of enabled state). "optimizing" = active and currently serving optimized output.'=>'Filter by lifecycle state. "active" = enabled by the user. "inactive" = available but disabled. "available" = currently loadable on this site (regardless of enabled state). "optimising" = active and currently serving optimised output.','Module slug to toggle (e.g. "critical_css", "page_cache").'=>'Module slug to toggle (e.g. "critical_css", "page_cache").','List Jetpack Boost performance modules and submodules. Returns an array of { slug, active, available, optimizing }. Slugs use underscores (e.g. "critical_css", "page_cache", "image_cdn"). Pass slug to fetch a single module (returns a 0- or 1-element array; unknown slugs yield an empty array, never an error). Pass status to filter by active/inactive/available/optimizing. Use the returned slugs as input to jetpack-boost/set-module-status.'=>'List Jetpack Boost performance modules and submodules. Returns an array of { slug, active, available, optimizing }. Slugs use underscores (e.g. "critical_css", "page_cache", "image_cdn"). Pass slug to fetch a single module (returns a 0- or 1-element array; unknown slugs yield an empty array, never an error). Pass status to filter by active/inactive/available/optimising. Use the returned slugs as input to jetpack-boost/set-module-status.','Return a single module by its slug (e.g. "critical_css", "page_cache"). Unknown slugs yield an empty array.'=>'Return a single module by its slug (e.g. "critical_css", "page_cache"). Unknown slugs yield an empty array.','Set Boost module status'=>'Set Boost module status','Return the most recent Jetpack Boost speed score for the home URL. Returns { mobile, desktop, timestamp, is_stale, has_history }. mobile/desktop are integers 0-100 (Google PageSpeed scale) or null when no score has been recorded. timestamp is a Unix epoch in seconds marking when the score was last measured, not when it last changed. is_stale=true means the latest score is older than 24 hours or invalidated by a site change; agents should request a refresh from the Boost UI before quoting it. has_history=false means no scores have been recorded yet.'=>'Return the most recent Jetpack Boost speed score for the home URL. Returns { mobile, desktop, timestamp, is_stale, has_history }. mobile/desktop are integers 0-100 (Google PageSpeed scale) or null when no score has been recorded. timestamp is a Unix epoch in seconds marking when the score was last measured, not when it last changed. is_stale=true means the latest score is older than 24 hours or invalidated by a site change; agents should request a refresh from the Boost UI before quoting it. has_history=false means no scores have been recorded yet.','Abilities for inspecting and managing Jetpack Boost performance modules, speed scores, and page cache.'=>'Abilities for inspecting and managing Jetpack Boost performance modules, speed scores, and page cache.','Get Boost modules'=>'Get Boost modules','Invalid nonce response from WordPress.com.'=>'Invalid nonce response from WordPress.com.','Encode the items before sending.'=>'Encode the items before sending.','Force unlock the queue before checkout.'=>'Force unlock the queue before checkout.','Number of items to checkout from the queue.'=>'Number of items to checkout from the queue.','Pop items from the queue instead of checking out.'=>'Pop items from the queue instead of checking out.','Use memory-based checkout instead of fixed item count.'=>'Use memory-based checkout instead of fixed item count.','Mark as external collaborator'=>'Mark as external collaborator','Failed to update interstitials state.'=>'Failed to update interstitials state.','Interstitial state for the product. True means that the user has seen the interstitial for the product.'=>'Interstitial state for the product. True means that the user has seen the interstitial for the product.','Key-value pairs of product